{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Plucked off in her mouth.</b> I say that it was male — therefore Scripture sometimes calls it in the masculine and sometimes in the feminine, because every יוֹנָה in Scripture is feminine, as in ״כְּיוֹנִים עַל אֲפִיקֵי מָיִם רֹחֲצוֹת״ (Song 5), ״כְּיוֹנֵי הַגֵּאָיוֹת כֻּלָּם הֹמוֹת״ (Ezekiel 7), and likewise ״כְּיוֹנָה פוֹתָה״ (Hosea 7)." "<b>Plucked off.</b> Snatched. And its midrash aggadah (Bereshit Rabbah 18) is a term of sustenance; and they interpreted ״בְּפִיהָ״ as a term of utterance — she said: Let my sustenance be bitter as an olive in the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, and not sweet as honey in the hand of flesh and blood."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:59.876175987Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}